    "created_at": "2023-03-04T02:30:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-04T02:30:40Z",
    "body": "If I'm reading the spec correctly, this means that if an input element has `disabled` or `readonly` it is not mutable and will not get the popover activation behavior.\r\n\r\nI think that with `disabled` it makes sense to not run popover activation, but with `readonly` I'm not sure - but I also don't know why anyone would use `readonly` on the button input element types...",
